! TiddlyRPG Core

The shared format layer of the TiddlyRPG repo family:

* Type hubs (Person, Location, Organisation, Event, Item, ...) with colours,
  view templates, macros, filters, styles and editor snippets (`$:/plugins/tiddlyrpg-core/...`)
* Language packs: displayed texts come from `$:/tiddlyrpg/language/<code>/...` and follow
  `$:/language`; en-GB and de-DE included, missing keys fall back to en-GB
* Rulesets and campaign settings: data plugins of the types `ruleset` (rules terms) and
  `setting` (calendar, currency), one of each active, chosen under ControlPanel -> Settings ->
  TiddlyRPG; listed under ControlPanel -> Plugins
* Calendar engine: dates are formatted and calculated from the calendar data tiddler named in
  `$:/config/tiddlyrpg/calendar` (e.g. Harptos from `tiddlyrpg-setting-forgottenrealms`); without it
  dates are shown as entered
* Currency engine: prices with coins of the currency named in `$:/config/tiddlyrpg/currency`
  (field `price: 50 gp`), the hub "Currency" with a converter; without a currency prices are
  plain numbers
* Rules engine: the macros `<<unit>>`, `<<dice>>`, `<<damage>>` and `<<term>>` show the terms of
  the active ruleset in the rules language - per wiki, one language for all or per domain,
  separately for what is shown and what is written (ControlPanel -> Settings -> TiddlyRPG);
  lengths and weights are converted. Shortcuts such as `<<wis save>>` come with the ruleset; the
  hub "Ruleset" lists every term in every language
* Hints below the title on what does not fit: a price without coin, a term or unit the ruleset
  does not know, a macro that nothing defines (not in the published copy)
* Functions `trpg.visible` (what the active view sees), `trpg.dead` (deceased/destroyed),
  `trpg.t`, `trpg.title`, `trpg.plural` in `$:/plugins/tiddlyrpg-core/functions`
* Views: public, a player, or the DM, chosen in the page control "View"; a tiddler tagged
  `Secret` is visible to the DM and to the players of the player characters it is tagged with
  (tag `Player`, or a former one with the field `player`); an event with a player character
  belongs to the campaign; in the text `<<secret "Theren">>` locks a section,
  `<$secret for="Theren">…</$secret>` a part
* Sections of a body: dated sections, spots and locks in a short form (`<<date>>`) and a block
  form (`<$date>…</$date>`), nested in any order, with hints on what does not count
* tw5-graph schema (field edge types + graph templates) for the relation graphs
* Dates: one syntax for all types in the field `date` (sections separated by `,`, spans with
  `/`, `.` unknown, `..` forever); in the body of an event `<<date>>` marks where each
  section begins, with the date, an optional caption (wikitext, also with macros) and the
  locations of that section
* Event timeline (widget `trpg-timeline`): the events of a tiddler or of the `Event` hub as an
  interactive vertical timeline in the calendar of the wiki, next to the event table; on a
  tiddler its own dates as a band behind the events
* Locations: a location lies in another one (field `location`) or is a part of it (a spot
  `<<spot "Name">>` in its body); the path of parents below the title, who is at a location,
  the events of the places within; references to spots with `<<spotlink>>`; a `location` to a
  location tagged `Secret` is a secret presence, missing in the views that do not see it
* Maps of a location: the map image (field `map`) as a graph with the spots placed on it,
  battle maps (field `battlemap`, or per spot) as tabs

Consumed by the campaign wikis as a pinned plugin
(`git+https://github.com/WkoD/TiddlyRPG-Plugins.git#<version>`).

The format layer is edited only in the plugin repo.
